EAGL animation reconstruction

The scalar/vector and quaternion delta decoders, compressed channels,
compound/event channels, animation bank, skeleton poses, run/pose blending,
raw/cycle channels and allocator/scratch support and associated headers adapt the public NFS Most Wanted
reconstruction by dbalatoni13/nfsmw, licensed under CC0 1.0 Universal.
Reference revision: 1f2cdd7996791c81a580b3f7b36b44d4f9f6719c
Reference: https://github.com/dbalatoni13/nfsmw/tree/1f2cdd7996791c81a580b3f7b36b44d4f9f6719c/src/Speed/Indep/Src/EAGL4Anim
The upstream license is preserved in LICENSE.nfsmw.

The Rising Sun adaptation used AI assistance from Codex and Claude Code.
Original target symbols/instructions determine accepted signatures, layouts and
behavior. Reference member names remain attributed reconstruction names.
See docs/Animation.md for verification and remaining uncertainties.

Skeleton pose methods, BoneMask, base default methods, stateless control methods and target-only channel
bodies are reconstructed from original instructions, using attributed reference
interface names where available. Empty reference methods are not treated as
implementations. Later animation extensions used Codex assistance; Claude Code
assisted the initial scalar/vector delta decoders.

The private matrix callback adapts this project's independently reconstructed
matrix multiplication expression sequence and retains its original temporary-copy
behavior and argument order.
